{
  "id": "06053_misugosu",
  "headword": "{見過|みす}ごす",
  "reading": "みすごす",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to overlook, to miss",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "godan",
    "ending": "す",
    "stem": "{見過|みす}ご"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to overlook, to miss, to fail to notice",
      "explanation": "To not notice something that should have been seen or caught. Can be unintentional."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to let pass, to turn a blind eye",
      "explanation": "To deliberately ignore or tolerate something, often a problem or wrongdoing."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06053_misugosu_ex1",
      "japanese": "うっかり{見過|みす}ごしてしまった。",
      "english": "I accidentally overlooked it.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06053_misugosu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{重要|じゅうよう}なエラーを{見過|みす}ごしてしまった。",
      "english": "I overlooked an important error.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06053_misugosu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{小|ちい}さな{変化|へんか}を{見過|みす}ごさないように{注意|ちゅうい}してください。",
      "english": "Please be careful not to miss small changes.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06053_misugosu_ex4",
      "japanese": "この{問題|もんだい}は{見過|みす}ごせない。",
      "english": "This problem cannot be ignored.",
      "notes": "Potential negative form",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06053_misugosu_ex5",
      "japanese": "{今回|こんかい}は{見過|みす}ごしてあげよう。",
      "english": "I'll let it slide this time.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06053_misugosu_ex6",
      "japanese": "{不正|ふせい}を{見過|みす}ごすわけにはいかない。",
      "english": "I can't just turn a blind eye to wrongdoing.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Compound verb: {見|み}る + {過|す}ごす. Pattern: Xを{見過|みす}ごす (overlook X / ignore X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates resulting state. {見過|みす}ごしている = 'has overlooked' or 'is ignoring.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{見過|みす}ごすわけにはいかない (cannot let it slide)\n・{見過|みす}ごせない{問題|もんだい} (a problem that cannot be ignored)\n・うっかり{見過|みす}ごす (accidentally overlook)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS: {見落|みお}とす emphasizes failing to notice, while {見過|みす}ごす can include deliberately ignoring.",
